#require "../access.eflint".

Open Var current-time Identified by Int // e.g. unix time, provided by execution environment
Fact timestamp Identified by Int Derived from write-obligation.timestamp, written.timestamp
Fact owner Derived from write-obligation.owner

// in this scenario, the owner of a resource can give permission to another actor
// for using its resource in a process action that results in some output data
// this kind of permission comes with the obligation to report the analysis result
// the owner provides a resource identified that needs to be (over)written
// with the analyis results within a certain time window (say 24 hours) starting from the read action
// this way, a provenance trail can be established even when processing happens remotely

Act allow-processing Recipient actor' Related to resource, resource'
  Holds when owner-of(resource, actor) && Enabled(create(actor, resource'))
  Syncs with create(actor, resource') // create the new resource for storing the processing result
  Creates compute(actor = actor', input = resource, output = resource')

Extend Act compute // a version of read that demands the provenance trail build-up
  Creates write-obligation(actor, owner-of.owner, output, current-time)
            When owner-of.resource == input

Fact deadline Identified by 86400 // 24 x 3600
Duty write-obligation Holder actor Claimant owner Related to resource, timestamp
  Violated when current-time > timestamp + deadline
             && Not(Exists written: written.actor == actor && written.resource == resource
                                    && written.timestamp <= timestamp + deadline)

// proof that the resource has been written by the actor
Fact written Identified by actor * resource * timestamp

// having the write-obligation permits writing
// executing the action removes the obligation
// (the ledger is used to record the fact that the obligation ever existed)
Extend Act write Holds when write-obligation()
  Creates written(timestamp = current-time)

// the duty is also considered violation if the resource has been written with bogus content
// as `proven` by an external observation that the written content does not match some expectation
// e.g. purpose, anonymisation, aggregation, quality, etc.
Extend Duty write-obligation 
  Violated when bogus(written)

Fact bogus Identified by written

Act declare-bogus Recipient actor' Related to resource, timestamp
  Holds when owner-of() && written(actor=actor')
  Creates bogus(written(actor=actor'))
